\title{Complete proof of \code{\verb~|expf_correctlyRounded~} and issue 22 repository layout with reusable \code{\verb~|Analysis/~}}
\taxon{Change}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{antigravity}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{changelog}
\tag{expf}
\tag{tmd}
\tag{architecture}
\import{base-macros}

\p{Closes [prob-48KJ](prob-48KJ) and addresses issue \issue{22}. Session [ses-ZW59](ses-ZW59).}
\ul{
\li{\strong{Complete proof of \code{\verb~|expf_correctlyRounded~} (zero \code{\verb~|sorry~}).} Both remaining open lemmas (\code{\verb~|correctAt_main_pos~} and \code{\verb~|correctAt_main_neg~}) for \code{\verb~|math::double_eval::expf~} are proved across all \code{\verb~|2³²~} binary32 inputs and all four C rounding modes (\code{\verb~|cModes~}), depending solely on \code{\verb~|[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]~} with zero \code{\verb~|sorry~}, zero \code{\verb~|native_decide~}, and no external oracle axioms. The main path combines UB-free exact range reduction (\code{\verb~|RangeReduction.lean~}), certified table bounds (\code{\verb~|TableBounds.lean~}, \code{\verb~|≤ 2⁻⁵³~}), binary64 Horner rounding error (\code{\verb~|HornerError.lean~}), combined product error (\code{\verb~|ProductError.lean~}, \code{\verb~|≤ 2 · 10⁻¹⁵ · exp x~}, analytically closing 25 256 675 tiny and near-underflow inputs), 103 isolated pointwise inputs (\code{\verb~|PointwiseExceptions.lean~}, including \code{\verb~|0xC236BD8C~}, \code{\verb~|0x3B7FFFFF~}, \code{\verb~|0xBB7FFFFF~}, and \code{\verb~|0xB3000000~}), and 278 619 always-odd Chebyshev-L1 SLZ certificates across 61 chunks (\code{\verb~|MainPath/Tmd/Certs/Chunk00..60.lean~}) verified in Lean's kernel (\code{\verb~|decide +kernel~}). See [ins-NHOJ](ins-NHOJ).}
\li{\strong{Issue \issue{22} layout and reusable \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Analysis/~}.} Reorganised \code{\verb~|LibcMath/~} so each function sits at the top level (\code{\verb~|LibcMath/Expf.lean~} + \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Expf/{Generated,ShortPaths,MainPath,Plans,Statement,Examples}~}), generated files never share a directory with hand-written files (\code{\verb~|Expf/Generated/~} and \code{\verb~|Expf/MainPath/Tmd/Certs/~}), and shared infrastructure is split into \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Libc/~} (was \code{\verb~|Core/~}), \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Framework/~}, \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Testing/~} (was \code{\verb~|Check/~} and \code{\verb~|Oracle/~}), and \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Analysis/~}. Factored four function-independent numerical-analysis modules into \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Analysis/~}: \code{\verb~|RangeReduction.lean~}, \code{\verb~|Horner.lean~}, \code{\verb~|RoundingTransfer.lean~}, and \code{\verb~|ChebTmd.lean~}.}
\li{\strong{Extractor, open-obligation guard, template, and linear history.} Updated \code{\verb~|ast2lean~} (\code{\verb~|extract/~}) to target \code{\verb~|LibcMath.Libc~} and \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Expf/Generated/~}, and freshly re-extracted all six \code{\verb~|expf~} plans at LLVM commit \code{\verb~|e1a5f92db023~}. Added \code{\verb~|scripts/check-open.py~} (also callable via \code{\verb~|lake run checkOpen~}) and generated \code{\verb~|OPEN.md~} (currently 0 open obligations), added \code{\verb~|templates/FunctionTemplate/~} and [note-adding-a-function](note-adding-a-function), renamed \code{\verb~|CLAUDE.md~} to \code{\verb~|AGENTS.md~}, restored the multi-plan short-path proofs removed in \pr{21}, and linearised \code{\verb~|main~} with GitHub linear-history enforcement.}
\li{\strong{Verified.} \code{\verb~|lake build LibcMath checkrange difftest-expf-model~} completes (10 473 jobs, zero \code{\verb~|sorry~}); \code{\verb~|lake run checkOpen~} confirms \code{\verb~|OPEN.md~} has 0 open obligations; \code{\verb~|bash extract/test/run_tests.sh~} passes; \code{\verb~|scripts/difftest-expf.sh~} reports 0 mismatches across \code{\verb~|double_eval~}, \code{\verb~|double_eval_fma~}, \code{\verb~|integer_eval~}, and \code{\verb~|float_eval_cr_rn~}; \code{\verb~|checkrange~} passes against both MPFR and Lean oracles; and \code{\verb~|journal-build~} reports no diagnostics.}
}
